<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>Using Function Notation to Compare Linear and Exponential Functions</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01505</md:content-id>
    <md:title>Using Function Notation to Compare Linear and Exponential Functions</md:title>
    <md:uuid>141e7e23-978d-48c1-93c1-bf979f7d5d14</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section class="numbered-exercises" id="sect-00001"><title>Cool Down</title>
<para id="para-00001">The function <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> is given by <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>10</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>, and the function <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>g</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> is given by <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>g</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:msup><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math>. For each question, show your reasoning.</para>
<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise id="exer-00001">
  <problem id="prob-00001">
    <para id="para-00002">Which function reaches 50 first?</para>
    </problem><solution id="sol-00001">
  <para id="para-00003">Compare your answer: </para>
    
    <para id="para-00004"><m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>53</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> and <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>g</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>32</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>, so <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> reaches 50 first.</para>
  
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->


<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise id="exer-00002">
  <problem id="prob-00002">
    <para id="para-00005">Which function reaches 100 first?</para>
    </problem><solution id="sol-00002">
    
    
  
  <para id="para-00006">Compare your answer: </para>
    
    <para id="para-00007"><m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>7</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>73</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> and <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>g</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>7</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>128</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>, so <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>g</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> reaches 100 first.</para>
  
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->
</section>
</content>
</document>